kernelci-core/
kernelci-api/
kernelci-pipeline/
.ruff_cache/

# the workspace; the old tree's work/ is gone with that tree
var/
*.log
__pycache__/

# docs: only the runbook is public; everything else (tool deep dives, SOW
# snapshot, upstream evidence, issue/PR drafts, internal dev notes) stays
# local - internal working material, not ready/meant to be published
docs/*
!docs/RUNBOOK.md

# local-only, off the run path: `proto/` is the frontend prototype the real
# console in `lib/gui/design/` replaced, and `include/` is the C++ interface spec
# - declarations only, cited by 20 docstrings but read by nothing.  `proto/` is
# recovered from git history (`git checkout 6a5fc44 -- proto`) if ever needed.
# See docs/FILE-AUDIT.zh-CN.md
proto/
include/

# the design pair: `design/kernelci-design.html` is the design of record and
# `tools/design_extract.py` is its only reader (`--check` compares the board with
# `lib/gui/design/style.py`).  They are one decision, not two: the extractor
# without the board dies on its first line.  Local working material - what ships
# is the extraction, and `style.py` says so.  `tools/check_hooks.py` is NOT part
# of this pair and stays tracked.
design/
tools/design_extract.py

# ...but the gate's own fixtures ARE part of the tree: `verify_callback_body.py`
# opens these two consoles, so the `*.log` rule above must not swallow them.
!tools/gate/fixtures/*.log

